invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: the Initial key's constructor records the low byte of the
  session's description of the CPU and leaves the byte above it as the
  schedule's storage held it, so CH_CPU_AVX512 reads whatever the stack
  held, and gcm.c picks the 512-bit kernel from it. bin/aes_runtime_test
  fills the key with 0xff before the call and requires both schedules'
  second byte to hold the value's.

--- old
    s->cpu_high = (uint8_t)(cpu >> 8);
--- new
